## Evidence discipline

- Treat current literature notes, synthesis and the novelty audit as evidence boundaries, not as permission to fabricate datasets, benchmarks, sample sizes, budgets, metrics, results, implementation availability or causal identification.
- Do not manufacture a conventional setting merely to make a plan look complete. Keep an unresolved execution detail in the structured plan, then describe it once in the Proposal as a concrete pre-execution validation, mitigation, or fallback when it materially affects feasibility.
- The novelty audit may constrain claims and required baselines.  Never expose its internal terms (T4.5, Level 0–3, true_collision, candidate ID, fingerprint, pass_to_experiment) in the main Proposal or claims document.

