## One shared research-argument framework

For UTD, CCF-A and Hybrid, the final Proposal must clearly cover these seven research functions. They are an argument checklist, not a compulsory seven-heading layout. Use canonical headings when they improve navigation; merge adjacent functions when that makes the argument more coherent.

1. Research Motivation and Core Problem
2. Prior Research, Gap and Key Challenges
3. Proposed Approach and Design Rationale
4. Research Questions, Claims and Hypotheses
5. Research Design and Evaluation
6. Expected Contributions and Implications
7. Risks, Limitations and Execution Plan

